From: SF2000 Linux Port <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: serialize stateful bFLT relocation passes

The MIPS bFLT implementation keeps pending HI16 instructions, their original
contents, and the current image limit in architecture-global storage.  Those
caches are reset at the start of every load_flat_file() relocation pass.

SF2000 starts several bFLT services concurrently.  One exec can therefore
clear or replace the relocation state while another exec is between a HI16
and its LO16, potentially leaving an executable with mismatched address
halves.  Serialize the loaders before relying on the pending-HI16 cache to
pair every relocation in an image.

Serialize complete top-level MIPS bFLT loads.  Recursive shared-library loads
remain inside the same top-level critical section, so they do not deadlock.
Other architectures do not pay for the MIPS state workaround.

--- a/fs/binfmt_flat.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_flat.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 #include <linux/flat.h>
 #include <linux/uaccess.h>
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
+#include <linux/mutex.h>
 
 #include <asm/byteorder.h>
 #include <asm/unaligned.h>
@@ -48,6 +49,15 @@
 #include <asm/addrspace.h>
 #endif
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_MIPS
+/* arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h has one pending-HI16 cache per kernel. */
+static DEFINE_MUTEX(mips_flat_reloc_mutex);
+#define mips_flat_reloc_lock() mutex_lock(&mips_flat_reloc_mutex)
+#define mips_flat_reloc_unlock() mutex_unlock(&mips_flat_reloc_mutex)
+#else
+#define mips_flat_reloc_lock() do { } while (0)
+#define mips_flat_reloc_unlock() do { } while (0)
+#endif
 #ifdef CONFIG_MIPS
 extern void sf2000_progress_mark(const char *name, unsigned int kind,
 		unsigned int value);
@@ -1108,7 +1116,9 @@ static int load_flat_binary(struct linux_binprm *bprm)
 	stack_len += (bprm->envc + 1) * sizeof(char *);   /* the envp array */
 	stack_len = ALIGN(stack_len, FLAT_STACK_ALIGN);
 
+	mips_flat_reloc_lock();
 	res = load_flat_file(bprm, &libinfo, 0, &stack_len);
+	mips_flat_reloc_unlock();
 	sf2000_flat_value("flat-load-file-ret", (unsigned int)res);
 	if (res < 0)
 		return res;
